<name>Paris protests and disruption Sat 17 Oct to Sun 18 Oct (updated 10-18 12:30)</name>
<description>Saturday recap: clashes in central Paris into the early evening. A crowd was dispersed at Concorde around 17:48, a barricade burned near Réaumur-Sébastopol, and wild marches formed near La Madeleine and Place Vendôme, with looting at the Galeries Lafayette on Boulevard Haussmann at about 17:53. Interior Minister Nuñez counted 110,000 people in Paris and 550,000 across France. The prefecture counted 191 arrests in Paris by 18:00, an ICI headline later gave 195, and CNews and franceinfo headlines gave about 1,200 arrests nationwide. The mayor of Paris said whole streets were heavily damaged. Twenty-five métro stations were closed on Saturday and I found no report of when they reopened. Central Paris gatherings were banned until 22:00. I found no incident report with a location after about 18:00. Unofficial map built from press reports; check the Préfecture de police and RATP before travelling.</description>
